cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, together with the book whose frameworks it develops."
title: "FMGCF-EWC: an operational, vulnerability-aware early warning chain for climate-related health risk"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
authors:
  - family-names: Sargiotis
    given-names: Dimitrios
    affiliation: "School of Civil Engineering, National Technical University of Athens"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3644-4561"
repository-code: "https://github.com/uomoathens/fmgcf-ewc"
abstract: >-
  Runnable, tested early warning chain developed from the FMGCF-EWC, MVI-HGP
  and FairGLA frameworks of Blueprints for Future Living (Springer, 2027). It
  combines a cross-border regional graph, federated learning across countries
  with optional client-level differential privacy, a Gaussian-process
  vulnerability index, warnings whose threshold depends on regional
  vulnerability, fairness focused on missed warnings, and verification scores
  with bootstrap confidence intervals. It is evaluated on synthetic data and on
  weekly mortality (Eurostat) and temperature (Open-Meteo) data for the NUTS 2
  regions of Greece, Italy, Spain and Portugal.
keywords:
  - early warning systems
  - climate and health
  - heat-related mortality
  - federated learning
  - differential privacy
  - vulnerability index
  - Gaussian process
  - algorithmic fairness
  - graph learning
  - Eurostat
